<title>USA: Dow Chemical to buy Eastman unit.</title>
<headline>Dow Chemical to buy Eastman unit.</headline>
<dateline>MIDLAND, Mich. 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dow Polyurethanes said Wednesday it agreed to purchase Eastman Chemical Co's THANOL polyols business, which is used in spray foams for construction such as commercial and industrial roofing.</p>
<p>The transaction is expected to be finalized by the end of the second quarter this year. No manufacturing assets are included in the sale. Terms of the sale were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Dow Polyurethanes is a subsidiary of Dow Chemical Co, which produces chemicals, plastics, hydrocarbons and energy, and consumer specialties, including agricultural and consumer products.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
